{"id": "20540324", "revid": "24650158", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20540324", "title": "Ivan Iskra", "text": "Ivan Ivanovych Iskra () (died July, 14, 1708) was a renegade colonel of Poltava Regiment of Ukrainian Cossacks (1696\u20131703). Iskra belonged to the anti-Hetmanate coalition led by Vasily Kochubey. In late 1707, Kochubey and Iskra delivered a denunciation letter to the Tsar's court that accused Ivan Mazepa of initiating talks with Stanislaus Leszczynski of Poland and Charles XII of Sweden.\nPeter I did not believe the letter and beheaded them both. Later, when the Tsar realized that they were correct, they were reburied near the Refectory Church in Kiev Pechersk Monastery."}
